Hi Rusty

I've been playing with your latest nfsim stuff and found some issues
with the kernel.
You mentioned that you found some problems, so you might already have
fixed these.

Please add these patches to your patch-queue.

First is a patch to make ip_nat_core.c and ip_nat_proto_udp.c
skb_ip_make_writable() the correct amount of bytes, sizeof(pointer)
isn't any good. This makes nfsim stop complaining about incorrect
checksums.

Second and third are two patches to make ip_nat_ftp.c / ip_nat_irc.c use
skb_header_pointer instead of trying to access the tcpheader directly.
ip_nat_mangle_tcp_packet() calls skb_ip_make_writable(pskb,
(*pskb)->len) but that's too late.

nfsim is great but can be a little annoying sometimes, you fix one bug
and then it finds another... :)

--=20
/Martin

